# Trivy vulnerability allowlist for the fentwums/oss-cad-suite toolchain image.
#
# Scope and rationale. The image vendors the upstream OSS CAD Suite distribution on an Ubuntu
# base; tool distribution is an explicit non-goal of this extension (see docs/articles/limitations.md).
# The entries below are fixable HIGH-severity advisories inherited from that upstream surface — the
# base OS, the bundled Python toolchain, and the bundled `pebble` Go binary — none of which is the
# extension's own code. They are suppressed so the Trivy gate stays fail-closed on what this project
# controls: any CRITICAL finding, and any new HIGH not listed here, still fails the build.
#
# Maintenance. This list is pinned to the current image digest. When the image is rebuilt against
# updated upstreams, re-run the scan and prune entries whose fixed version has landed:
#   docker run --rm -v /var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock aquasec/trivy:0.70.0 \
#     image --severity HIGH,CRITICAL --ignore-unfixed --scanners vuln fentwums/oss-cad-suite:latest

# -- OS packages (Ubuntu base) -------------------------------------------------
CVE-2026-45447   # openssl (libssl3t64)

# -- Python toolchain (pip, setuptools, Flask, Werkzeug) -----------------------
CVE-2021-3572    # pip
CVE-2022-40897   # setuptools
CVE-2023-30861   # Flask
CVE-2024-34069   # Werkzeug
CVE-2024-6345    # setuptools
CVE-2025-47273   # setuptools

# -- Bundled Go binary `pebble` (golang.org/x/net and the Go standard library) -
CVE-2026-25680
CVE-2026-25681
CVE-2026-27136
CVE-2026-27145
CVE-2026-33811
CVE-2026-33814
CVE-2026-39820
CVE-2026-39821
CVE-2026-39836
CVE-2026-42499
CVE-2026-42502
CVE-2026-42504
CVE-2026-42506
